    <statement><p>Convert the following point from cylindrical to rectangular coordinates:
<me>\left(5, \frac{4 \pi}{3}, -0.5\right).</me></p>
<p><m>(x,y,z) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert> Usage: </alert>To enter a point, for example <m>(x,y,z)</m>, type "(x, y, z)".</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(-2.5,-4.33013,-0.5\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>r=5</m>, <m>\theta=\frac{4 \pi}{3}</m>, and <m>z=-0.5</m>. Thus,
<me>\begin{array}{rcl}
x \amp =\amp  r\cdot \cos(\theta)=5\cdot \frac{-1}{2} \\
y \amp =\amp  r\cdot \sin(\theta)=5\cdot \frac{-\sqrt{3}}{2} \\
z \amp =\amp  -0.5
\end{array}</me>


</solution>
